# Codestral-22B-v0.1, cleaned up for benchmark use.
# https://huggingface.co/mistralai/Codestral-22B-v0.1
#
# INSTRUCT-ONLY, and narrower than the rest of the fleet: `ollama show` reports
# capabilities ['completion'] -- no thinking AND no tools. Both are correct for
# Codestral v0.1. Leave AI_ASSISTANT_MODEL_THINK unset or Ollama rejects the
# request, as with Devstral and Qwen3-Coder-Next.
#
# Built FROM the blob to clear the inherited SYSTEM block (an empty
# SYSTEM """""" is ignored by ollama create -- verified).
FROM /san/models/blobs/sha256-60f3f171ce03488943bb63f56e149d48c984b27c6aceb7141c3f65dae9c0b6a8

# --- TEMPLATE: declared deliberately -------------------------------------
# Correct Mistral v3 format -- <s>, [SYSTEM_PROMPT], [INST]/[/INST], </s>.
# Nothing to fix, so it is reproduced verbatim rather than re-derived from the
# GGUF. (Contrast the Qwen files, which drop TEMPLATE because those builds were
# carrying a pasted Qwen3-Coder template.)
#
# Note it has no [SUFFIX]/[PREFIX] handling, so Ollama exposes no "insert"
# capability and fill-in-the-middle is unavailable -- the card does document
# FIM via encode_fim. Irrelevant for code review; relevant if this tag is ever
# pointed at a completion tool.
TEMPLATE """<s>{{ if .System }}[SYSTEM_PROMPT]{{ .System }}[/SYSTEM_PROMPT]
{{ end }}{{ range .Messages }}{{ if eq .Role "user" }}[INST] {{ .Content }} [/INST]{{ else if eq .Role "assistant" }}{{ .Content }}</s>
{{ end }}{{ end }}"""

# --- Stops -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Already correct on this build: </s> is the genuine Mistral EOS and the only
# stop declared. Nothing to strip here -- unlike the Devstral build, which had
# seven Cline/Roo agentic tags bolted on.
PARAMETER stop "</s>"

# --- Samplers --------------------------------------------------------------
# The card prescribes NOTHING -- no temperature, top_p, top_k, min_p or
# repetition_penalty. So there is no card value to align to.
#
# What the build carried was temperature 0.6 / top_k 20 / top_p 0.8: the same
# triple found on Qwen3-32B, Qwen3-Coder-Next and Devstral-2-123B. That is
# contamination from a Qwen Modelfile, not a choice made for Codestral.
# Replaced with neutral values so temperature -- which the harness controls --
# is the only thing shaping the distribution.
PARAMETER top_p 1.0
PARAMETER top_k 0
PARAMETER min_p 0

# Left at 1.05. This one probably IS copied from the Qwen builds too, but it is
# very mild, the card offers no alternative, and dropping repetition damping
# entirely on a 22B writing a long repetitive markdown table has its own risk.
# Changed only if a run shows looping.
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.05

# --- Context: the harness exceeds this model's limit -----------------------
# 32768 is the hard ceiling -- llama.context_length in the GGUF, and Codestral
# v0.1 is a 32k model. The build already had this right.
#
# The benchmark sends num_ctx 65536, i.e. TWICE what this model supports, which
# overrides the line below. In practice it has not bitten: run #112 used 9,146
# prompt + 2,251 output = 11,397 tokens, roughly a third of the real window.
# But nothing warns you if a future run generates more, and positions past
# 32768 were never trained.
#
# Same class of issue as Qwen3-32B (ceiling 40960), and unlike Devstral, where
# 65536 is a deliberate reduction from a 262144-capable model. Flagged rather
# than silently special-cased: a per-model num_ctx breaks cohort uniformity and
# the source budget is (num_ctx - num_predict - 500) * 2.5 chars, so lowering
# num_ctx without lowering num_predict truncates the codebase listing instead.
PARAMETER num_ctx 32768

# Carried over from the existing build and inert for benchmark runs -- the
# workflow always sends temperature. The card recommends no value, so there is
# nothing better to put here.
PARAMETER temperature 0.6

# --- No SYSTEM block ------------------------------------------------------
# Previously: "You are a helpful assistant". The card does not mention system
# prompts as supported or recommended for this model at all. Task framing
# belongs in review_prompt.md and the patcher prompt, which are SHA-tracked in
# every scorecard; a Modelfile SYSTEM appears nowhere in the artefact.
#
# Two card notes worth recording: Codestral-22B-v0.1 "does not have any
# moderation mechanisms", and it ships under the MNPL-0.1 licence, which is
# non-production. Fine for benchmarking; check before any other use.

# --- Standard SYSTEM prompt (fleet-wide) ----------------------------------
# Identical on every model in the benchmark, so the system prompt stops being an
# uncontrolled variable. Before this, the fleet ran a mix: "/no_think Be concise
# and skip chain-of-thought" on the six Qwen3.x builds, an expert-engineer
# persona on Qwen3-Coder-30B, a "detailed answers" persona on Qwen3.5-122B and
# Qwen3-32B, "Reasoning strength: high" on Muse-Glimmer-30B, and nothing at all
# on Gemma-4-31B -- none of it recorded in any scorecard.
#
# A non-empty SYSTEM replaces an inherited one, so this works whether the FROM
# line points at a blob or a tag. Keep it byte-identical across every model:
# the moment one differs, cross-model comparison is confounded again.
#
# Task instructions do NOT belong here -- they live in review_prompt.md, which
# is SHA-tracked in every scorecard. This line is persona only.
SYSTEM """You are an expert computer programmer with an eye for detail, who loves to provide high quality answers."""
